---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import InstallJourney from "../components/InstallJourney.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/site";
---
<Marketing title="Quickstart" description="Run Goshikq locally with the Rust runtime, a mock model, and goal verification. No paid API keys." path="/quickstart/">
  <section class="hero wrap prose">
    <p class="kicker">Quickstart</p>
    <h1>Hello, verified</h1>
    <p class="lede">No OpenAI or Anthropic key is required. Install the v1.0.0 runtime, start it, then run hello-agent. The example must print <code>verification: VERIFIED</code>.</p>
    <InstallJourney />
    <h2>What the agent checks</h2>
    <p>hello-agent stores a greeting and the goal reads that snapshot. If the model only says Ada was greeted and never calls <code>record_greeting</code>, verification does not pass.</p>
    <pre class="install"><code>status:        COMPLETED
verification:  VERIFIED</code></pre>
    <h2>Studio</h2>
    <pre class="install"><code>cd apps/studio && bun install && bun run dev
# http://127.0.0.1:3000 → Executions → hello-agent</code></pre>
    <p><a href={withBase("/download/")}>Install options</a> · <a href={withBase("/docs/getting-started/")}>Docs getting started</a> · <a href={withBase("/docs/typescript-sdk/")}>TypeScript SDK</a></p>
  </section>
</Marketing>
